### Goal Model Decomposition

---

#### **Goal Tables**

| Goal ID | Goal Title                 | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|---------|----------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1      | Deliver Resources to Agent | Ensure resources are collected from storage and delivered to the requesting agent. | -                  | Achieve   | -        | Primary mission objective: deliver resources. |
| G2      | Collect Resources          | Retrieve required resources from storage locations.                   | FALLBACK(G2.1; G2.2, G2.3) | Perform   | G1       | Sequential with fallback for battery failure during collection. |
| G2.1    | Determine Storage Order    | Calculate the optimal order of storages based on waiting time and path. | -                  | Query     | G2       | Required to prioritize storage visits for efficiency. |
| G2.2    | Collect from Each Storage  | Retrieve resources from each storage in the determined order.         | #                  | Perform   | G2       | Parallel execution for multiple storages using different robots. |
| G2.3    | Recharge and Reassign      | Return to recharging station if battery drops below 10% during collection. | -                  | Perform   | G2       | Fallback action when battery is critically low during collection. |
| G3      | Deliver Resources          | Transport collected resources to the requesting agent’s location.     | FALLBACK(G3.1; G3.2, G3.3) | Perform   | G1       | Sequential with fallback for battery failure during delivery. |
| G3.1    | Deliver All Resources      | Make multiple trips to deliver all resources to the destination.      | #                  | Perform   | G3       | Parallel execution if multiple robots are used for delivery. |
| G3.2    | Return to Checkpoint       | Return to checkpoint and reassign remaining task if battery <30%.     | -                  | Perform   | G3       | Fallback action when battery is low during delivery. |
| G3.3    | Alert Sector Manager       | Trigger alert and report failure to the sector manager.               | -                  | Perform   | G3       | Final fallback if checkpoint return fails. |

---

#### **Task Tables**

| Task ID | Task Title             | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location         | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|------------------|------------------|---------------|
| AT1     | Navigate to Storage    | Move the robot to the designated storage location.                   | AND      | Storage Facility | [1, n]           | Required for resource retrieval from each storage. |
| AT2     | Request Resource       | Send a message to the storage specifying the required resources.     | AND      | Storage Facility | 1                | Ensures the storage knows which items to retrieve. |
| AT3     | Wait for Retrieval     | Wait until the requested resources are retrieved by the storage.     | AND      | Storage Facility | 1                | Required to ensure resources are ready for pickup. |
| AT4     | Deliver to Destination | Transport resources to the requesting agent’s specified location.    | AND      | Requesting Agent Location | [1, n]           | Ensures timely delivery of resources. |
| AT5     | Return to Recharge     | Navigate back to the recharging station and recharge the battery.    | AND      | Recharging Station | 1                | Required when battery drops below 10% during collection. |
| AT6     | Return to Checkpoint   | Navigate back to the checkpoint and hand over remaining resources.   | AND      | Checkpoint       | 1                | Required when battery drops below 30% during delivery. |
| AT7     | Alert Sector Manager   | Send an alert message and report failure to the sector manager.      | AND      | Control Center   | 1                | Final fallback action if checkpoint return fails. |

---

### **Logical Relationships**

- **G1 -> G2; G3 [Sequential]**  
  - **Justification**: The mission requires first collecting resources (G2) and then delivering them (G3) in sequence.

- **G2 -> G2.1; G2.2 [Sequential with Fallback]**  
  - **Justification**: Determining storage order (G2.1) must precede resource collection (G2.2). If battery fails during G2.2, fallback to G2.3 (recharge and reassign).

- **G2.2 -> AT1; AT2; AT3 [AND]**  
  - **Justification**: Each storage visit requires navigation, requesting resources, and waiting for retrieval in sequence.

- **G2.2 -> Multiple Robots [Parallel]**  
  - **Justification**: When multiple storages are involved, different robots can handle parallel collection tasks to reduce mission time.

- **G3 -> G3.1; G3.2 [Sequential with Fallback]**  
  - **Justification**: Delivering resources (G3.1) must occur before handling battery failure (G3.2). If battery fails during delivery, fallback to G3.2.

- **G3.1 -> AT4 [AND]**  
  - **Justification**: Each delivery trip requires transporting resources to the destination.

- **G3.2 -> AT6; AT7 [Sequential with Fallback]**  
  - **Justification**: If battery is low during delivery, return to checkpoint (AT6) and reassign. If this fails, trigger an alert (AT7).

---

### **Summary**

The goal model ensures that resources are collected from storages in an optimal order, delivered to the requesting agent, and handles battery failures through fallback mechanisms. Parallel execution is used for multiple storages and delivery tasks, while sequential execution ensures proper task ordering. Fallbacks address critical scenarios like low battery during collection or delivery.
